[x] Map every DSL, charter and objective field to its pattern in the spec =v5-mapping $Rewrite specifications/ontology.md as the mapping, one row per field of actions.schema.json plus charter frontmatter and objective files, each to its pattern in ontology docs/domain.md. Settled already: id is the IRI; name is rdfs:label; state per ontology Decisions 4 and 5, with blocked as waiting on something outside; priority, plus-tag contexts, predecessors and the sequential marker as in the domain table; alias is a Designative Name; description is a Descriptive ICE about the action; parent and children are has continuant part; scheduled and due times are conditions. Still to settle here, by searching for standard terms before any choice: duration; created and completed times (the act and its temporal region); external schedule id and occurrence key (iCal machinery, maybe the W3C RDF Calendar terms); charter lifecycle states; and the workspace facts now in the ws namespace (source file and line, workspace identity), which are not domain meaning and must not be minted if a standard term exists. Also settle the IRIs of the extra nodes V5 needs (conditions, measurements, bearers, acts): deterministic, derived from the action's UUID and the node's role, so exports diff cleanly. Strip the v4 property names from the descriptions in actions.schema.json. PROGRESS 2026-10-01: first draft of the layout in specifications/ontology.md (uncommitted), worked example reasons consistent under HermiT. Checked: designates is cco:ont00001916 (name to thing); ical:uid is a datatype property, ical:rrule and ical:recurrenceId are object properties. Waiting on the human's review of the open questions. DONE 2026-10-01: specifications/ontology.md rewritten; settled with the human as Decision 44; groceries example aligned to one condition per Performance Specification (ontology 0be0cbd); schema descriptions stripped of v4 names.$ !1 ^2026-10-01T20:22 %2026-10-01T22:07 #01a0faa2-17cb-77f8-99a0-34646ff8128c
[x] Review the v5-mapping draft and its open questions $FOR THE HUMAN. Draft in specifications/ontology.md, uncommitted so the diff is readable: conventions first, then one table per file kind, a worked example that reasons consistent with V5 under HermiT, and six open questions with recommendations. The ones that most need you: 1, Dublin Core for descriptions, created times and source files rather than CCO patterns (recommended: Dublin Core; no question reasons over them); 3, workspace locators, the only place a ClearHead-owned vocabulary may survive (no standard term for a line number found); 5, recurrence rules, where the W3C calendar vocabulary needs structured nodes, not RRULE text (leaning: RRULE text on a Descriptive ICE). Yes to the recommendations lets the shapes and fixture start.$ !1 +human ^2026-10-01T20:44 %2026-10-01T22:07 #01a0fab6-aeaa-7294-b4d0-12b21c5e3c7a
